# Exposure
option.EXPOSURE_MODE=Exposure mode
option.EXPOSURE_MODE.comment=Steady sets exposure from the light where you stand: the time of day, the weather, the world, and (with cave adaptation) the sky light and block light at your position, so looking around never changes it. Metered measures the brightness on screen, so looking at something bright darkens the picture and looking at something dark brightens it. Off keeps one exposure per world, set for clear midday, so nothing changes it: nights and unlit caves are as dark as their light makes them; EV still adjusts it. The Nether and the End always use Metered. Center weight, tendency and quick response apply only to Metered
value.EXPOSURE_MODE.0=Metered
option.STEADY_LOCAL_ADAPTATION=Cave adaptation
option.STEADY_LOCAL_ADAPTATION.comment=Steady mode only. How much exposure adapts to the light where you stand, such as a cave or a torch-lit room. 0 turns it off, so exposure follows only the time of day, the weather and the world; 1 adapts fully, which brightens caves a lot and makes daylight seen from inside glaring
value.EXPOSURE_MODE.1=Steady
value.EXPOSURE_MODE.2=Off
option.EXPOSURE_VALUE=EV
option.EXPOSURE_VALUE.comment=Overall brightness, in stops. Each +1 doubles the brightness and each -1 halves it
option.AVERAGE_EXPOSURE_CENTER_WEIGHT=Average exposure center weight
option.AVERAGE_EXPOSURE_CENTER_WEIGHT.comment=How much the middle of the screen counts when measuring brightness. 0 weighs the whole screen evenly
option.AVERAGE_EXPOSURE_STRENGTH=Average exposure strength
option.AVERAGE_EXPOSURE_STRENGTH.comment=How much exposure follows the scene's brightness over time. 0 keeps exposure fixed; 1 keeps the average screen brightness always the same
option.AVERAGE_EXPOSURE_TENDENCY=Average exposure tendency
option.AVERAGE_EXPOSURE_TENDENCY.comment=How much bright parts of the screen count when measuring brightness. Higher counts them more, which makes the picture darker; lower makes it brighter
option.EXPOSURE_DARK_LIMIT=Dark world exposure limit
option.EXPOSURE_DARK_LIMIT.comment=Holds back exposure from brightening dark scenes on Umbra and Cinder, and at night on worlds without air, so they stay dark. As a multiplier: 0 turns the limit off; higher keeps them darker
